+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BpMAbpL5XA5WJLEqZUkkFe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# T2: Real-Time Markdown Collab Server\n2\t\n3\t## Category\n4\tgreenfield/complex\n5\t\n6\t## Timeout\n7\t30 minutes\n8\t\n9\t## Description\n10\tBuild a WebSocket-based collaborative Markdown editing system with:\n11\t1. HTTP/WebSocket server managing documents and broadcasting edits\n12\t2. OT (Operational Transform) based conflict resolution so simultaneous edits converge\n13\t3. REST API for document CRUD with SQLite persistence via better-sqlite3\n14\t4. Version history - every edit stored, any past version retrievable\n15\t5. Must handle 10 concurrent clients without corruption\n16\t\n17\t## Starting State\n18\t- All configuration files provided (package.json, tsconfig.json, .eslintrc.cjs, vitest.config.ts)\n19\t- Database schema provided (schema.sql)\n20\t- Test file provided (tests/collab.test.ts) with 45 tests\n21\t- Empty src/ directory with .gitkeep\n22\t\n23\t## Requirements\n24\t\n25\t### Source Files to Implement\n26\t\n27\t**src/db.ts** - Database setup using schema.sql, connection factory\n28\t\n29\t**src/models.ts** - TypeScript interfaces for Document, Version, Operation (insert/delete with position)\n30\t\n31\t**src/ot.ts** - Operational Transform logic:\n32\t- `applyOperation(content, op)`: Apply an operation to document content\n33\t- `transformOperation(op1, op2)`: Transform op1 against op2\n34\t- `validateOperation(op, contentLength)`: Validate operation bounds\n35\t- Operations: `{ type: 'insert', position: number, text: string }` and `{ type: 'delete', position: number, count: number }`\n36\t- Transform rules: adjust positions based on prior operations\n37\t\n38\t**src/routes.ts** - Express REST routes:\n39\t- POST /docs - Create document\n40\t- GET /docs - List documents\n41\t- GET /docs/:id - Get document\n42\t- PUT /docs/:id - Update document\n43\t- DELETE /docs/:id - Delete document\n44\t- GET /docs/:id/versions - List version history\n45\t- GET /docs/:id/versions/:version - Get specific version\n46\t\n47\t**src/ws.ts** - WebSocket server:\n48\t- Manages rooms (one per document)\n49\t- On connect: validate document exists, send current state as `{ type: 'sync', content, version }`\n50\t- On operation: validate, apply, transform against concurrent ops, broadcast to room\n51\t- Track document version for OT\n52\t- Messages: `{ type: 'operation'|'ack'|'sync'|'error', ... }`\n53\t\n54\t**src/server.ts** - Combines Express + WebSocket server:\n55\t- Exports `createApp(dbPath?)` returning `{ app, server, wss, db, start, stop }`\n56\t- HTTP and WS on the same port\n57\t- `start(port?)` returns actual port (use port 0 for random)\n58\t- `stop()` cleanly shuts down all connections\n59\t\n60\t## Validation\n61\t```bash\n62\tnpm run build   # TypeScript compiles\n63\tnpm run lint    # ESLint passes\n64\tnpm test        # All 45 tests pass\n65\t```\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DdQvo1fuuMamNQQrEXD2gX","session_id":"e246dbcb-e9b4-4717-8ce2-8446dd5eb5a5","uuid":"20e9309b-e51e-48f7-9025-426f97636d4a","timestamp":"2026-07-25T01:19:19.294Z","subagent_type":"conclave:code-reviewer","task_description":"Review OT and WS correctness"}
